{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws","id":729901,"title":"Vampire Laws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-26T14:32:54-07:00","id":729901,"title":"Vampire Laws","content":"I'm looking to make a legal system among the kindred of Dallas, but I don't know anything about laws.<br /> One suggestion I got was to make a constitution to regulate the feudalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8900-urakesh","name":"Urakesh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:18:07-07:00","id":730028,"title":"","content":"Well, your legal system is going to be heavily influenced by whatever covenant is in charge. An Invictus Prince is going to be very different from a Carthian one, for the most part. Have you decided who's in charge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:32:39-07:00","id":730121,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't expect most vampiric legal systems to be complex. If a prince doesn't want his subjects doing something he must tell them a) what it is b) how they'll work out who did it and c) what will happen to who did it. It may be subjective, but the prince probably doesn't care how future authorities would interpret his laws because he has no intention of losing his position. Of course that's how an Invictus prince might do it. Carthians probably would have a proper constitution. That's assuming they get round to writing one up before or after seizing power, but it's something to aim for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 10-26-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:50:00-07:00","id":730233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=730028#post730028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, your legal system is going to be heavily influenced by whatever covenant is in charge. An Invictus Prince is going to be very different from a Carthian one, for the most part. Have you decided who's in charge?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's gonna be Invictus dominated, with the Carthians probably having one member powerful enough to introduce the idea of a feudal-constitution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8900-urakesh","name":"Urakesh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T16:29:05-07:00","id":730303,"title":"","content":"Constitutions and feudalism don't mix. Feudalism requires that the people (subjects) are property of their ruler. Constitutions were created to completely throw that out. That isn't to say that people have no rights under feudalism. Their rights are determined by the ruler, however. A feudal society is a dictatorship, benevolent or not. I'm not sure that vampires are actually using feudalism. It is probably some quasi-feudalism. A constitutional monarchy has all the noble titles as well. It would be up to you to decide where you want to fall between those two ideas.<br /> <br /> I think a legal system starts with defining the rights of the people subject to the laws. What are people entitled to? What are people allowed to do? What limitations can be placed upon people? What is the procedure to do so? There may be different strata in a society with groups of people having different answers to those questions. I would avoid the minutia in codifying every law and just go with those basics I mentioned. You can add the small details on the fly. As long as they are within the broad guidelines previously established, there shouldn't be a major issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T17:19:27-07:00","id":730467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=730303#post730303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constitutions and feudalism don't mix. Feudalism requires that the people (subjects) are property of their ruler. Constitutions were created to completely throw that out. That isn't to say that people have no rights under feudalism. Their rights are determined by the ruler, however. A feudal society is a dictatorship, benevolent or not. I'm not sure that vampires are actually using feudalism. It is probably some quasi-feudalism. A constitutional monarchy has all the noble titles as well. It would be up to you to decide where you want to fall between those two ideas.<br /> <br /> I think a legal system starts with defining the rights of the people subject to the laws. What are people entitled to? What are people allowed to do? What limitations can be placed upon people? What is the procedure to do so? There may be different strata in a society with groups of people having different answers to those questions. I would avoid the minutia in codifying every law and just go with those basics I mentioned. You can add the small details on the fly. As long as they are within the broad guidelines previously established, there shouldn't be a major issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that a powerful Carthian convinced the ruling Invictus to draft a legal document governing how the danse macabre is done.<br /> Like, ways of claiming territory, stuff like that. I don't know what stuff would be right to put in it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8900-urakesh","name":"Urakesh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T17:50:21-07:00","id":730529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urakesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=730467#post730467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that a powerful Carthian convinced the ruling Invictus to draft a legal document governing how the danse macabre is done.<br /> Like, ways of claiming territory, stuff like that. I don't know what stuff would be right to put in it though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a question of the characters. There's a lot that child potentially be covered there. What's the political philosophy of the Carthian? How are the Invictus running things before, and how would they try to undermine this constitution for their own means? What geographic, political, and cultural issues are there in the city, and how do those define the current state of affairs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T18:20:42-07:00","id":730576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=730303#post730303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constitutions and feudalism don't mix. Feudalism requires that the people (subjects) are property of their ruler. Constitutions were created to completely throw that out. That isn't to say that people have no rights under feudalism. Their rights are determined by the ruler, however. A feudal society is a dictatorship, benevolent or not. I'm not sure that vampires are actually using feudalism. It is probably some quasi-feudalism. A constitutional monarchy has all the noble titles as well. It would be up to you to decide where you want to fall between those two ideas.<br /> <br /> I think a legal system starts with defining the rights of the people subject to the laws. What are people entitled to? What are people allowed to do? What limitations can be placed upon people? What is the procedure to do so? There may be different strata in a society with groups of people having different answers to those questions. I would avoid the minutia in codifying every law and just go with those basics I mentioned. You can add the small details on the fly. As long as they are within the broad guidelines previously established, there shouldn't be a major issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magna Carta?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T20:23:51-07:00","id":730922,"title":"","content":"Whatever the case the following should always be true:<br /> <br /> The Prince of Dallas must be a Cowboys fan, any disparaging word about the team within earshot of the Prince is harshly punished. Interfering with the game is harshly punished. Feeding at the grounds of the Cowboys' stadium must only be upon fans of the opposing team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T08:46:41-07:00","id":732345,"title":"","content":"Hi there Urakesh!<br /> <br /> I have played in two games where the ST has provided a list of laws to the PCs and am playing in a third where the laws exist, but are not written down or freely told to new vampires. They are still enforced though. Anyway, I searched through my PC and found some old text files of the laws of those previous games. They are not the best formatted though, so my apologies in advance.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">4 ghouls max<br /> your thrals crime is your crime<br /> gun limits - consealable, no full auto, supressed<br /> no murder of kindred, no diablary, no assault on kindred, no embrace without princes permition<br /> respect masqurade<br /> un-known domain is not domain<br /> respect other's domain<br /> haven is owner's domain<br /> each kindred can have at least one haven<br /> prince has domain everywhere he has purview<br /> unbound ask permition to ghoul<br /> embrace outside city to bring into city is embrace in the city<br /> poaching - see domain<br /> police/law envolvement - see masqurade<br /> new arivals present within 48 hours or leave<br /> tell new arivals about 48 hours<br /> respect elysium<br /> museum of nautral history after dark is elysium<br /> old town is elysium<br /> metropol hotel in old town is prince's land, no other warning<br /> prince may grant mercy<br /> all are not equal. preferencial treatment is often given to those who serve<br /> human witness to unnatural strength, speed, claws, changing, toughness, other - see masqurade<br /> repeated failed camera recordnings - see masqurade<br /> we share the night with others, do not start a war<br /> all within the prince's purview obey the prince, those who disagree - see 48 hours</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the case of the Metropol hotel, it turned out to be a neutral meeting ground for werewolves/mages/vamps to hash things out and avoid interspecies war. Obviously the Prince didn't want just any old random vampire interacting with the others.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> -= Traditions =-<br /> <br /> Dominion<br /> All of the territory of City is under Princes domain. The Prince determines the<br /> divisions of domain. A vampire who denies tribute to the Prince forfeits claim to the Blood.<br /> <br /> Destruction<br /> No vampire shall be put to Final Death without the decree of the Prince.<br /> <br /> Amaranth<br /> Kindred are forbidden from devouring the heartsblood of another vampire.<br /> <br /> Masquerade<br /> Do not reveal your true nature to those not of the Blood.<br /> Doing so forfeits you your claim to the Blood.<br /> <br /> Progeny<br /> Sire another at the peril of both yourself and your progeny.<br /> <br /> Deference<br /> Those who intend to remain in the City for any length of time are required to present themselves.<br /> <br /> Elysium<br /> Prince may declare location to be Elysium. Any sort of physical or mystical<br /> confrontation is strictly forbidden within Elysium.<br /> <br /> ================================================== =============================================<br /> <br /> -= Senechal's Notices to the Kindred =-<br /> <br /> Masquarade breach - to let humans know of the mystical nature of kindred.<br /> Expected punishment - death.<br /> <br /> Masquarade violation - to bring attention of the humans apon vampire affairs.<br /> If not suppressed by efforts of the purpotrator expected punishment - death.<br /> If suppressed some leniancy might be shown.<br /> <br /> Museum of Naturtal History after dark is Elysium.<br /> 421 Orchard Road above and below ground is Elysium.<br /> Old movie theater in Lockham is Elysium.<br /> Elysium is to be accesible.<br /> <br /> Some areas have been declared to be the fields.<br /> Any may take from there enough to sate the nights hunger.<br /> Expected punishment for interference - forced starvation.<br /> <br /> Do not start a confrontation with the Others.<br /> Expected punishment - whatever would apease the Others.<br /> <br /> Kindred may have four ghouls, other vampires may have one.<br /> Permission for more may be granted by regents.<br /> <br /> You may be held accountable for the crimes of your thrals.<br /> <br /> A kindred's known haven is his domain.<br /> <br /> Inform new kindred of the laws.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the above post, the distinction between 'kindred' and other 'vampires' is the invictus distinction between vampires who are part of a covenant and the unaligned. <br /> <br /> <br /> The basic legal framework of the current game I'm playing can be found here: [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/70989-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-1?p=70991#post70991\">LINK</a>] Scroll down to &quot;Byzantine Legal System.&quot; (link to the full write up is in my sig)<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, here is an outline version of the laws of one of the mage factions in the mage game I am running:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1. The Spirit of the Law - violators will be judged based on:<br /> a. Power<br /> b. Wisdom<br /> c. Well being of Baton Rouge<br /> 2. Messengers<br /> 3. Hospitality<br /> 4. The Duel Arcane will be respected<br /> 5. Put humans back where you found them after playing with them.<br /> 6. Responsibility for well being of thralls.<br /> 7. Sanctum<br /> 8. Recognition<br /> 9. Veil<br /> a. no killing humans with magic<br /> b. must have cause to kill humans<br /> c. must clean up your mess.<br /> 10. Magical Slavery (blood bond) - need permission for 3rd step.<br /> 11. Need Cassus Belli for Death of other magical beings (mages, vampires, werewolves, etc)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry I don't have time to elaborate, but I hope these rough text files will of some inspiration to you. Good luck with your game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 10-27-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T08:50:39-07:00","id":732355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=730576#post730576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magna Carta?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JNZosqiJISs\" target=\"_blank\"> I guess she really did die in vain...</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:26:54-07:00","id":733462,"title":"","content":"I'm calling it the Dictus Bellum<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> By this signing, the primogen and prince of the city of Dallas do establish laws to better preserve the society of the Kindred.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The domain of the Prince is by right of rank the whole of the city and its districts. The divisions of territory is to be determined by right of control, though the prince retains the right to give and revoke territories as his or her discretion.</li> <li>The respective governing kindred of each covenant may establish their own laws and statutes within their territory, as long as such laws do not contravene the articles of the Dictus Bellum, nor affect the affairs of other covenants.</li> <li>The Bishops of the Lancea Sanctum may impose tithes upon the subjects of their territories.</li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div><br /> criticisms welcome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8900-urakesh","name":"Urakesh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T20:49:12-07:00","id":733817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=730576#post730576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magna Carta?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was an example of a king giving rights to subjects. The US Constitution was new because it legally changed the people of a nation from subjects to citizens. A person born in Britain or one of her colonies was British and therefore a subject of the British crown. Such a person could not declare independence, a person was either a loyal subject or a traitor. US citizens can (and always could) give up citizenship to become citizens of another nation without penalty. Generally subjects can't move to another territory without permission. The life of a serf is the life of a slave with rights. A beautiful prison remains a prison.<br /> <br /> As to examples of things to cover:<br /> Territory - how to claim it, how to lose it, how invaders may be punished, how visitors must be treated<br /> Conflict - what are the rules of engagement, when self-defense is applicable (vampires getting shot is equivalent to mortals getting punched)<br /> Masquerade - ways to violate the Masquerade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T01:51:57-07:00","id":734103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urakesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws?p=733462#post733462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm calling it the Dictus Bellum<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> By this signing, the primogen and prince of the city of Dallas do establish laws to better preserve the society of the Kindred.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The domain of the Prince is by right of rank the whole of the city and its districts. The divisions of territory is to be determined by right of control, though the prince retains the right to give and revoke territories as his or her discretion.</li> <li>The respective governing kindred of each covenant may establish their own laws and statutes within their territory, as long as such laws do not contravene the articles of the Dictus Bellum, nor affect the affairs of other covenants.</li> <li>The Bishops of the Lancea Sanctum may impose tithes upon the subjects of their territories.</li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div><br /> criticisms welcome</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a pretty straightforward outline of a feudal(-ish) power structure. One thing which I think may be missing, however, is a statement of the prince's duties or responsibilities. Generally speaking, leaders have to offer something to their subjects in exchange for their obedience, particularly when those subjects form significant power blocks of their own. Enforcing the rule of law is a good start, since even most vampires probably don't want to live in a genuinely lawless society. Protection is another thing a prince might offer, both from outsider vampires who might try to make a move on local territories and from the various mortal institutions that might otherwise make unlife hard for the local kindred.<br /> <br /> Indeed, one thing I like about the second edition portrayal of the covenants is that they emphasize the Invictus' role as a &quot;conspiracy of silence&quot; who influence the mortal world in order to maintain the masquerade. It helps justify their position on top of the kindred totem pole, since they're ostensibly using the power and influence they accrue in order to preserve kindred society as a whole, rather than just wallowing in champagne swimming pools or whatever. Not that they can't do that too, but it's not the <i>only</i> thing they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:33:23-07:00","id":736672,"title":"","content":"You have territory is right of control, but nothing is given about conflict, so vampires could just kill someone for their territory. That seems a bit lax on law to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T02:17:03-07:00","id":737401,"title":"","content":"Maybe not. I mean, the Prince retains a veto on any territory. Maybe the Prince is ok with his subjects fighting as long as they keep it within limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T03:13:16-07:00","id":737485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urakesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/729901-vampire-laws#post729901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking to make a legal system among the kindred of Dallas, but I don't know anything about laws.<br /> One suggestion I got was to make a constitution to regulate the feudalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thinking when it comes to these things is as follows.<br /> <br /> Make the standard three traditions.<br /> 1. Masquerade<br /> 2. Embrace<br /> 3. Soul Sucking.<br /> <br /> Let's say I'm running with Prince Bob. Bob is a pragmatic prince who realizes that beating people over the head for simply embracing is going to cause more issues than he can deal with so he mods the second Tradition as follows.<br /> <br /> 2. Those with territory may embrace two Childe. They may not embrace any more until one of the two have been killed off. Kindred who embrace without territory will have both themselves and their childe executed.<br /> <br /> Bob's reasoning is that making the Embrace outright illegal is going to cause the kindred of the city to have far more skeletons in the closet than is normally needed and will eventually blow up in his face. By limiting both the number of Childe and restricting the ability to embrace to the &quot;holders of territory&quot; (AKA Kindred Elders and Faction Leaders), He confirms the status of the movers and shakers while keeping the population situation low.<br /> <br /> Now after this, Start coming up with historical moments to justify why the Prince enacted certain laws. A Crone attempting to kill the Prince via Blood Magic would most likely result in Blood Magic either made illegal or highly restricted (With the LS supervising Crone rites). Laws don't come out in a vacuum. Something happened to put them into place. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T09:18:52-07:00","id":738541,"title":"","content":"I imagine kindred laws often work like laws in Ankh-Morpork, in Discworld; the rules are <i>there</i>, procedures and precedents and responsibilities ad nauseum, going back decades or centuries. It's just that since the leader of the city is an unapolagetic dictator, (and so much of the civic authority is unapologetically dishonest) it's understood that those rules are only valid as long as they remain functional or as long as they don't run counter to the will of The Man.<br /> <br /> Civic control issues, (like feeding and territory in the kindred's case), and most day-to-day rules are extremely simple and obvious, because the system values stability over fairness. Otherwise, the law is basically there for political players who want/need to use it as a weapon/shield/field of battle, or possibly a scourge against an apolitical foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 10-29-2015, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}